{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/947591-a-very-simple-question","id":947591,"title":"a very simple question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-10T01:02:16-07:00","id":947591,"title":"a very simple question","content":"What are the time limitations on war-form in second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:18:06-07:00","id":947601,"title":"","content":"Well it's called the Killing Form now instead of War Form (being warriors was always more of a Garou thing, the Forsaken are hunters). But, to answer your question, a werewolf can safely maintain Gauru form for a number of turns equal to her Stamina in Hishu form + her Primal Urge. After that she must change forms or fall into Death Rage. If she does not change forms, she must roll Resolve + Composure. If she succeeds she gets one more turn in Gauru form and then falls into Wasu-Im (soft rage). If she fails, she immediately falls into Basu-Im (hard rage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date: